<title>JAPAN: Japan's LTCB to set up leasing venture in Vietnam.</title>
<headline>Japan's LTCB to set up leasing venture in Vietnam.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd (LTCB) said on Friday it has been given the go-ahead by the Vietnamese government to set up a leasing joint venture in Hanoi.</p>
<p>The venture will be capitalised at $10 million. LTCB, LTCB's affiliate Japan Leasing Corp, and Manila-based Asian Development Bank will each put up 20 percent of the capital, while the remaining 40 percent will be provided by the state-owned Vietcombank, a bank spokesman said.</p>
<p>LTCB expects the new firm to start operations in Hanoi in early 1997.</p>
